<!--
  Nuclei of the Glauber Monte Carlo (CAP::GlauberDb, models/Glauber). One NUCLEUS element per nucleus type, found
  by its name (GENERATION:NUCLEUS_A:NAME and NUCLEUS_B:NAME of GlauberGenerator). Nuclei can be added or changed
  here; the file read is GlauberGenerator:DB_0:FILE (default Glauber/NucleusDb.xml, in $CAP_DATABASE_PATH).
  NucleusDbEditor.py (at the top of CAP) edits it in a table and checks it.

  Attributes (lengths in fm):
    name          name of the nucleus type (e.g. Pb, Au2rw)
    A, Z          numbers of nucleons and protons
    radialType    radial density (see NuclearDistribution): 0 exponential, 1 three-parameter Fermi (3pF),
                  2 three-parameter Gaussian (3pG), 3 Hulthen (deuteron), 4 Hulthen with the neutron opposite to
                  the proton, 5 ellipsoid, 6 nucleon configurations read from a file (He3, H3, He4, C, O: the
                  files of TGlauberMC in Glauber/NucleonConfigurations), 7 deformed (box method),
                  8 deformed (beta2, beta4), 9 proton Gaussian, 10 proton double Gaussian, 11 3pF with distinct
                  proton and neutron parameters, 12 3pF reweighted (r0, r1, r2), 13 as 11 reweighted, 14 as 8
                  reweighted, 15 harmonic oscillator
    radius, skin, w                      radius, skin depth and w parameter of the proton density
    neutronRadius, neutronSkin, neutronW those of the neutron density (default: those of the protons)
    beta2, beta4  deformation parameters (default 0)
    r0, r1, r2    parameters of the reweighting of the types 12, 13 and 14 (default 0)
    a, b          parameters of special profiles (default 0)
    maxRadius     largest radius of the nucleons (default 3 x 1.2 A^(1/3))
    comment       source of the parameters

  Uranium (U): Heinz and Kuhlman, nucl-th/0411054, with radius = 6.8 x 0.91 and w = 6.8 x 0.26.
-->
